<title>UK: Bayer unit prices 375 mln mark convertible.</title>
<headline>Bayer unit prices 375 mln mark convertible.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bayer Corp USA, a subsidiary of Bayer AG, has given an 87.47 percent issue price to its 375 million mark five-year convertible bond, lead manager Deutsche Morgan Grenfell said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The bond, which pays an annual one percent coupon, was given a conversion ratio of 61.27 percent, a 25 percent premium.  </p>
<p>The yield-to-maturity is 3.80 percent.</p>
<p>The bond, listed in Frankfurt and Luxembourg, is callable after two years. Fees totalled 2.50 points, split 1.00 point management and underwriting and 1.50 points selling concession.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7718</p>
